### Leave out

- Any business with a job title containing coach, coaching, consultant, consulting, psychologist, recruiter, or recruitment.
- Employees and project managers at PLC contractors: they are not buyers and they are not owner-led.
- National house-builders and their site teams: purchasing decisions sit in head office, not with the MD on the ground.
- Local authority and public-sector in-house construction teams: no commercial mandate, no purchasing authority.
- Anyone Pam has already spoken to or is actively working with, even if they no longer appear in her CRM.
- Businesses outside Yorkshire and the Humber unless Pam decides to expand geography in a later phase.
- Any business sector Pam has named as a personal 'will not take', or that falls under a current non-compete.
- Sole traders with no team: the Profit System requires a team to work with. No headcount means no lever to pull on the Control or Value pillars.

- **300 to 600** Target list size in Sales Navigator before outreach begins. Aim for the upper end before filtering by 'posted in last 30 days' to keep the active pool above 150
- **30%+** Connection acceptance rate to hit. Below this, test a different message or tighten the title filters. Above this, the targeting is working.
- **10%+** Reply rate of accepted connections to aim for. One reply in ten accepted is the floor. Below it, the opening message needs reworking, not the list.

> **Watch these two numbers in the first two weeks:** Run the first 20 to 30 connection requests and track two things only: how many accept, and how many reply to the follow-up message. If acceptance drops below 30%, the title or industry filter is too broad and pulling in people who do not recognise themselves in the outreach. If replies drop below 10% of those who accepted, the opening message is the problem, not the list. Fix one variable at a time. Do not change the list and the message at the same time or you will not know which one moved the number.

